A4b. MECHANISM DISSOCIATION — the central biophysical result
     If calcium-site variants were pathogenic by destabilising the fold, they would
     show high ddG. They do not. Stratifying by burial rules out the obvious confound
     that Ca ligands are simply more solvent-exposed than other residues.
    ddG: Ca-consensus vs other cbEGF, buried (RSA<20%)
      Ca consensus: n=29 median=0.87   other cbEGF: n=174 median=3.62
      Mann-Whitney U=1104  p=1.28e-06  Cliff's delta=-0.562 [-0.704, -0.419]
    ddG: Ca-consensus vs other cbEGF, partial (RSA 20-50%)
      Ca consensus: n=47 median=0.78   other cbEGF: n=132 median=0.90
      Mann-Whitney U=2934  p=0.583  Cliff's delta=-0.054 [-0.231, +0.120]

